WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:05.580
Shameless has never been afraid to highlight
the debaucherous (and at times depressing)

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.740
exploits of the Gallaghers.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.220
And the man behind the most deranged moments
of all is the family patriarch, William H.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.540
Macy's Frank.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:13.380
Sure.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.200
Frank was drunk and strung out on pain meds
when he had Mex with his free-range neighbor,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.300
Karen Jackson, who also happens to be his
son's girlfriend and the daughter of Frank's

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.140
love interest.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.400
But if being under the influence was an excuse
for doing bad things, Frank Gallagher's soul

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.340
would be as pure as driven snow.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.180
Yes, Karen takes advantage of him.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.300
Yes, Frank has no idea Karen is filming the
act as payback for her father's cruel words.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.140
But it's fair to assume that any man with
half a brain cell - or half a soul - would

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.560
stop the sensual encounter right away.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.960
Instead, Frank is a willing participant.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.239
One of Frank's hallmark qualities is his uncanny
knack at taking a bad situation and making

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.400
it so much worse.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:55.060
Such is the case in the second season premiere,
when Frank nearly loses his youngest son in

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:55.740
a bet.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.740
Overhearing a drug dealer claiming he withstood
two taser blasts, Frank bets money he doesn't

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.400
have that the dealer is lying.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.900
Unfortunately for Frank, with the help of
the bartender's taser, the dealer proves he

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.000
can ride the lightning.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.320
“Where’s my ten grand motherf---er?”

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.840
Frank's only idea for making the money is
to panhandle while using his toddler son Liam

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.060
to garner sympathy.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.760
Unfortunately, that means Liam is with Frank
when the drug dealers grab him off the street.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.440
Since Frank has nothing else to give them,
the dealers take Liam as collateral.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:35.760
Frank callously shrugs off losing his son
in a bet, and doesn't even inform the other

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.220
Gallaghers what has happened until they confront
him.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:43.580
The terrible decision making, lack of responsibility,
and disregard for his family's safety all

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.460
reflect classic Frank parenting.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.460
Every man has his limit.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.760
For Frank Gallagher, that limit is incest…
barely.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:55.380
In Shameless' fourth season Frank learns the
punishment he's been putting his liver through

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.640
has left him with only a short time to live.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.040
“You know you’re dying, right?”

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.120
"we're all dying Doc."

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:05.620
"Soon."

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.760
Desperate to find a potential liver donor,
Frank reveals that he has another child that

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:15.209
the family is unaware of - an illegitimate
daughter named Sammi that he lost contact

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:17.460
with before any of the other kids were born.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.720
He tracks Sammi down and finds her living
in a trailer park with a child of her own.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:26.020
Rather than attempting to connect with his
daughter, Frank romances her, hoping it will

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:29.079
help him convince her to agree to donate part
of her liver.

00:02:29.079 --> 00:02:33.269
The two almost sleep together but for once
Frank actually avoids sex.

00:02:33.269 --> 00:02:34.260
Frank's plan almost works.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.900
Smitten with her manipulative father, Sammi
does exactly what Frank wants and offers to

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.800
be a liver donor.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.260
But once Frank learns she isn't a match, he
unintentionally reveals his dishonesty in

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.380
a frustrated rant.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.120
“What did you say?”

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.120
“Your daughter?”

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:57.140
Once again, Frank's brazen disregard for other
people hurts someone unlucky enough to be

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.160
related to him.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:04.019
When Frank finds out that Dottie, a.k.a. "Butterface,"
is slowly dying while awaiting a heart transplant,

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:07.460
he goes about wooing her in an attempt to
secure her government pension.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.940
That alone is pretty despicable, but Frank's
next moves became his new low point.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.939
One day, Dottie is taking a shower and the
phone rings.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:19.580
The hospital has found a matching donor, meaning
Dottie could receive her life-saving transplant.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.609
At least, she would have, had Frank not lied
to the caller by telling them that Dottie

00:03:23.609 --> 00:03:24.609
had already passed.

00:03:24.609 --> 00:03:29.060
This disgusting and incredibly self-centered
act is a death sentence for Dottie.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.760
Later, though he knows Dottie's weakened heart
can't handle it, he agrees to have sex with

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:34.260
her.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.040
Dottie dips before it's over.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.500
Where most people see a terminally ill child,
Frank sees as an opportunity.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:44.801
After a local news report highlights a cancer-stricken
child who was granted his wish to meet the

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:48.000
Chicago Bulls, Frank's devious wheels begin
to turn.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.020
This time it's Carl's turn to get caught up
in one of Frank's lies, as the pre-teen is

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.380
convinced by his father that he has cancer.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.840
Frank even goes so far as to shave the boy's
head, claiming it'll help the sun's healing

00:03:58.840 --> 00:03:59.919
rays get in.

00:03:59.919 --> 00:04:04.780
While the scam does not score the sports memorabilia
Frank was after, it does get Carl sent to

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.499
a special summer camp for terminally ill children.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:11.700
Carl complains a lot about the camp's lack
of a shooting range or ice cream sprinkles,

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:16.079
though he does use his presumed illness to
con a camp counselor in a way that would make

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.360
his dad proud.

